    "insights": [
      "Mixed product U_m·T_n linearization is ALREADY PROVEN in the gallery: DeMoivreOQ02OQ02.lean:107 theorem T_mul_U_product : 2·T_m·U_n = U_{m+n} + U_{n-m}, verified/original, 0-axiom, 0-sorry, full ℤ×ℤ generality via Int.induction_on. This OQ (U_m·T_n → two second-kind terms) is the same identity under m↔n relabeling (U_{m-n}=U_{n-m case via a=n,b=m).",
      "Answer to the OQ question (short vs long?): SHORT — the first-kind factor T_n forces exactly TWO second-kind terms U_{m+n}+U_{m-n}, mirroring 2·T_m·T_n=T_{m+n}+T_{m-n}, in contrast to the U·U product which is a genuine (min+1)-term sum (parent DeMoivreOQ02OQ02OQ01)."
    ],
